WEBVTT

00:00.180 --> 00:01.013
Instructor: In this video,

00:01.013 --> 00:03.210
I want to talk about the docs one more time,

00:03.210 --> 00:07.410
and, specifically, how we can learn more about git log,

00:07.410 --> 00:09.390
which just gives us a log

00:09.390 --> 00:12.060
of the commits in a given repository.

00:12.060 --> 00:14.220
And, as we saw when I added a very,

00:14.220 --> 00:16.500
very long commit message,

00:16.500 --> 00:18.180
we see the entire thing here.

00:18.180 --> 00:21.750
Now, shortly, we will want to to see these commits

00:21.750 --> 00:23.880
and, specifically, we're going to want to know

00:23.880 --> 00:25.890
these commit hashes.

00:25.890 --> 00:29.250
Spoiler, we need those in order to revisit a commit

00:29.250 --> 00:33.330
or undo a commit or check out or take a look at a commit.

00:33.330 --> 00:36.630
So, we need those, and if we have hundreds of commits

00:36.630 --> 00:39.120
and they all have these really long messages,

00:39.120 --> 00:41.250
that could be really frustrating.

00:41.250 --> 00:44.580
So, there are some options for how we use git log.

00:44.580 --> 00:46.410
So, let's go to the documentation.

00:46.410 --> 00:50.640
Let's go to reference and we'll find log.

00:50.640 --> 00:51.960
Here it is.

00:51.960 --> 00:53.280
I'll zoom in a bit.

00:53.280 --> 00:56.460
As we know, it shows us commit logs.

00:56.460 --> 00:58.980
But, there's quite a bit to how it works

00:58.980 --> 01:01.920
and there's a lot that I just don't know about it

01:01.920 --> 01:05.220
because I don't use most of these features.

01:05.220 --> 01:08.490
Just like with most git commands, there are tons of options.

01:08.490 --> 01:11.040
But, the one I'm interested in for now,

01:11.040 --> 01:12.630
we scroll down.

01:12.630 --> 01:14.610
Could also find it in the examples, I'm pretty sure,

01:14.610 --> 01:15.570
down at the bottom.

01:15.570 --> 01:18.120
I mean, look at this, this is crazy, the number of options.

01:18.120 --> 01:19.740
Just absurd.

01:19.740 --> 01:21.600
You can filter things out based on

01:21.600 --> 01:24.450
who wrote the commits, when they were committed.

01:24.450 --> 01:27.210
I believe you can order them differently,

01:27.210 --> 01:28.893
but what we are after-

01:30.360 --> 01:31.890
all right, well, I had to search for it,

01:31.890 --> 01:33.360
but this is what we're after.

01:33.360 --> 01:35.190
Formatting the commits.

01:35.190 --> 01:39.420
These flags, including --pretty allow us to pretty-print,

01:39.420 --> 01:41.640
or change, the format of the logs,

01:41.640 --> 01:43.440
how they're printed out.

01:43.440 --> 01:47.160
And, specifically, I usually use this option, one line.

01:47.160 --> 01:50.010
So, --oneline, which is actually shorthand

01:50.010 --> 01:54.630
for --pretty=oneline--abbrev commit.

01:54.630 --> 01:56.250
So, what does this mean?

01:56.250 --> 01:58.740
We can just take one piece at a time just to show you.

01:58.740 --> 02:02.130
Abbrev commit just shows us a shorter version

02:02.130 --> 02:03.780
of that commit hash.

02:03.780 --> 02:07.500
So, if I do git log --abbrev commit,

02:07.500 --> 02:09.600
it's hard to see much of a difference.

02:09.600 --> 02:12.330
But, here, I'm only getting a small piece

02:12.330 --> 02:13.500
compared to what we got before

02:13.500 --> 02:15.900
of each one of those commit hashes.

02:15.900 --> 02:18.540
But, we're actually after a bit more than that.

02:18.540 --> 02:20.520
We want one line.

02:20.520 --> 02:23.583
So, when we do --pretty=oneline,

02:24.630 --> 02:26.780
we have these different options for pretty.

02:27.637 --> 02:31.440
-: -pretty medium or fuller. Email.

02:31.440 --> 02:34.560
These are all things that we can format in the response,

02:34.560 --> 02:36.600
but I just wanted to show you one line.

02:36.600 --> 02:39.300
So, I like to use the shorthand, --oneline,

02:39.300 --> 02:41.730
but just know that it's actually shorthand

02:41.730 --> 02:45.423
for pretty=oneline and abbreviated commit.

02:46.650 --> 02:47.700
Let me just show that.

02:47.700 --> 02:49.950
git log --oneline.

02:49.950 --> 02:51.600
If I can type it correctly.

02:51.600 --> 02:54.000
And, there we go. Oh, so much better.

02:54.000 --> 02:55.110
Look at that.

02:55.110 --> 02:57.600
You can see one line of each commit message,

02:57.600 --> 03:00.180
which is why your first line of a commit message,

03:00.180 --> 03:01.740
even if it's a super long one,

03:01.740 --> 03:03.360
the first line should explain,

03:03.360 --> 03:04.980
it should summarize the commit.

03:04.980 --> 03:06.630
So, remove extra blank lines.

03:06.630 --> 03:07.680
That's what we did,

03:07.680 --> 03:10.980
even though, if we actually look at the entire message,

03:10.980 --> 03:12.690
there's a whole bunch of other stuff.

03:12.690 --> 03:13.950
It's very important,

03:13.950 --> 03:15.420
or I shouldn't say very important,

03:15.420 --> 03:16.620
but it's conventional.

03:16.620 --> 03:17.910
And, you should follow this pattern

03:17.910 --> 03:22.050
of having that first line be the summary of the commit,

03:22.050 --> 03:24.270
and then any other information comes afterwards

03:24.270 --> 03:26.370
separated by a return.

03:26.370 --> 03:28.500
So, git log --oneline.

03:28.500 --> 03:30.180
It's a nice way to look at our history

03:30.180 --> 03:33.007
and it's not just about, you know, remembering,

03:33.007 --> 03:35.100
"Oh, that was such a cute message I wrote."

03:35.100 --> 03:37.350
It's actually important to be able to do this

03:37.350 --> 03:40.470
because, shortly, we will be revisiting commits

03:40.470 --> 03:41.910
and we want to look at this history

03:41.910 --> 03:44.910
so that we can figure out where to time travel back to.

03:44.910 --> 03:47.160
But, for now, we're just reminiscing.

03:47.160 --> 03:48.420
So, that's git log.

03:48.420 --> 03:51.900
The docs, as I just showed you, are so overwhelming.

03:51.900 --> 03:54.060
I mean, there's so much you can do with git log.

03:54.060 --> 03:57.570
I have carpal tunnel just from scrolling down this page.

03:57.570 --> 03:59.550
So, don't feel intimidated.

03:59.550 --> 04:01.710
Or, do feel intimidated,

04:01.710 --> 04:04.680
but know that I am also intimidated by this page.

04:04.680 --> 04:06.530
Whichever makes you more comfortable.
